the go for an acc N with a value is a second value if
    [] is equal to the value
    and the second value is equal to N
    otherwise prolog (the value=[T|V])
    and an acc M = N + 1
    and the go for M with V is the second value.

the length of a list for a value is a number if
    the go for 0 with the value is the number.

